entries.description:
• Two fractions are said to be equivalent if they mark the same place on the number line.
• Starting with a fraction, the fractions obtained by multiplying its numerator and its denominator by the same whole number are equivalent to it. For example:
\frac{2}{3}=\frac{2\times7}{3\times7}
\phantom{\frac{2}{3}}=\frac{14}{21}
• Starting with a fraction, the fractions obtained by dividing its numerator and its denominator by a common factor are equivalent to it. For example:
\frac{12}{36}=\frac{12\div12}{36\div12}
\phantom{\frac{12}{36}}=\frac{1}{3}
• The simplest form of a fraction is the fraction obtained by dividing the numerator and denominator by their highest common factor.

\frac{1}{5}=\frac{1\times4}{5\times4}=\frac{4}{20}
\frac{1}{5}=\frac{1\times5}{5\times5}=\frac{5}{25}
\frac{1}{5}=\frac{1\times12}{5\times12}=\frac{12}{60}
\frac{1}{5}=\frac{4}{20}=\frac{5}{25}=\frac{12}{60}

The highest common factor of 21 and 24 is 3. Divide both the numerator and the denominator by 3.
\frac{21}{24}=\frac{21}{24}=\frac{7}{8}
So the simplest form of \frac{21}{24} is \frac{7}{8}.
